        "original_id": "d6059202-3fa5-583f-ae78-631228a1f4be",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Songs: \"Louisiana Saturday Night\"\n- People: Bob McDill, Mel McDaniel, Don Williams\n- Albums: \"I'm Countryfied\"\n- Topics: Country music, Country Music Hall of Fame\n\nFacts:\n- Bob McDill wrote the song \"Louisiana Saturday Night.\"\n- Don Williams originally sang \"Louisiana Saturday Night.\"\n- Mel McDaniel recorded \"Louisiana Saturday Night.\"\n- Mel McDaniel released \"Louisiana Saturday Night\" in March 1981 as the third single from his 1980 album \"I'm Countryfied.\"\n- Don Williams was born as Donald Ray Williams on May 27, 1939.\n- Don Williams was an American country singer and songwriter.\n- Don Williams was inducted into the Country Music Hall of Fame in 2010.\n- Don Williams died on September 8, 2017.\n- Don Williams was nicknamed the \"Gentle Giant\" of country music because of his straightforward smooth bass-baritone voice, soft tones, and imposing build.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "9f24496f-c93c-536e-b24f-4f187ecb1836",
        "text": "Page: Louisiana Saturday Night. Sentence: \"Louisiana Saturday Night\" is a song written by Bob McDill and recorded by American country music artist, Mel McDaniel.\nPage: Louisiana Saturday Night. Sentence: It was released in March 1981 as the third single from McDaniel's 1980 album, \"I'm Countryfied\".\nPage: Louisiana Saturday Night. Sentence: The song was originally sung by Don Williams.\nPage: Don Williams. Sentence: Don Williams (born Donald Ray Williams; May 27, 1939 – September 8, 2017) was an American country singer, songwriter, and 2010 inductee to the Country Music Hall of Fame.\nPage: Don Williams. Sentence: His straightforward yet smooth bass-baritone voice, soft tones, and imposing build earned him the nickname: \"Gentle Giant\" of country music.",
